Project Overview

"HomeServe" is a Flutter mobile app for a Home Services Platform (cleaning, maintenance,
repairs, moving, security systems, daily services, outdoor services). The app covers three
connected screens — Home, Service Listing, and Service Details — built entirely with
dummy data (no backend/API). This is an internship deliverable at Eduzah, so code quality,
clean architecture, and visual polish matter as much as functionality.

Architecture

Feature-based Clean Architecture, kept lightweight since there is no backend or business
logic beyond navigation and UI state:

lib/
├── main.dart
├── app/
│   ├── app.dart                 # MaterialApp, theme, routing setup
│   ├── theme/
│   │   ├── app_colors.dart
│   │   ├── app_typography.dart
│   │   ├── app_spacing.dart     # 8px grid constants
│   │   └── app_theme.dart       # ThemeData (light + dark)
│   └── routes/
│       ├── app_routes.dart      # route name constants
│       └── page_transitions.dart # custom PageRouteBuilder helpers
├── core/
│   ├── widgets/                 # shared reusable widgets (buttons, cards, rating stars, section headers)
│   └── utils/                   # extensions, responsive helpers
├── features/
│   ├── home/
│   │   ├── presentation/
│   │   │   ├── screens/home_screen.dart
│   │   │   └── widgets/          # hero_section, services_row, testimonial_card...
│   │   └── data/                 # dummy category + testimonial data
│   ├── service_listing/
│   │   ├── presentation/
│   │   │   ├── screens/service_listing_screen.dart
│   │   │   ├── cubit/service_listing_cubit.dart   # search/filter UI state
│   │   │   └── widgets/
│   │   └── data/                 # dummy service data per category
│   └── service_details/
│       ├── presentation/
│       │   ├── screens/service_details_screen.dart
│       │   └── widgets/
│       └── data/
└── models/
    ├── category_model.dart
    ├── service_model.dart
    └── review_model.dart

Each feature only has presentation/ + data/ (no domain layer, no repositories) —
there is no real data source to abstract, so an extra domain layer would be pure
boilerplate for this project. Keep it this simple unless a real backend is added later.

Tech Stack


Flutter (stable channel, latest version available at project start)
State management: Cubit (flutter_bloc package) — one Cubit per feature that
needs shared UI state (e.g. ServiceListingCubit for search/filter state,
ThemeCubit for light/dark mode). Keep Cubits thin: they hold and emit UI state
only, no business logic beyond what this dummy-data app needs.
google_fonts — Poppins (headings) / Inter (body)
cached_network_image — for all dummy network images (categories, services, avatars)
Navigation: named routes via Navigator + custom PageRouteBuilder helpers in
page_transitions.dart (no need for go_router — flow is linear: Home → Listing → Details)


Design System (must match exactly — no improvising new colors/values)


Colors: primary navy #0F2A4A, accent orange #F5843A, background white/off-white
#FAFAFA, secondary text gray #7A828A. Dark theme: background #121417, surface
#1E2124, text #F2F2F2, secondary text #9AA0A6, same orange accent in both themes.
Spacing: strict 8px grid (8, 16, 24, 32, 40) — no arbitrary padding/margin values.
Corner radius: 20-24px large cards (hero, gallery), 16px medium cards (service,
testimonial), 12px buttons, 8px chips/tags.
Shadows: soft, low-opacity, multi-layer — never harsh default BoxShadow with high
opacity/no blur.
Typography scale: H1 28/32, H2 22/26, H3 18/24, Body 14/20, Caption 12/16.


Conventions


Naming: PascalCase for widgets/classes, camelCase for variables/functions,
files in snake_case.dart.
One widget per file for anything reused more than once; inline private widgets
(prefixed _) only for single-use screen sections.
All dummy data lives in data/ files as static lists of typed models — never
hardcode strings/prices directly inside widget build methods.
Every screen must be wrapped to be responsive (use MediaQuery/LayoutBuilder
and relative sizing) — test against small phones and tablets mentally before
considering a screen done.


Do


Follow the folder structure and design system values above exactly.
Build every repeated UI element (service card, category card, testimonial card,
rating stars, CTA button, section header with "See All") as a reusable widget in
core/widgets/ or the owning feature's widgets/ folder.
Use the Hero widget with a shared tag (e.g. service-image-${service.id}) on the
service image in both the Listing card and the Details header, so the transition
between them animates smoothly.
Implement page transitions via a custom PageRouteBuilder (fade + slight slide-up,
~250ms, Curves.easeOutCubic) used consistently for all navigation — not the
Flutter default slide transition.
Implement dark mode via a ThemeCubit emitting ThemeMode + two ColorSchemes
(light/dark) as defined above, toggle placed in the Profile tab or app bar.
Use BlocBuilder/BlocSelector to rebuild only the widgets that depend on a given
Cubit's state — never wrap an entire screen in a BlocBuilder if only one small
widget needs it.
Use const constructors wherever possible.
Keep every text block on Service Details short and scannable (e.g. description
capped at 2-3 lines with a "Read more" expansion) — do not let any single section
push the screen height unreasonably.
Add a short doc comment at the top of each new file explaining its purpose.


Don't


Don't add new packages without checking they're justified by this file's tech stack.
Don't use setState for anything beyond a single private widget's own trivial local
UI state (e.g. an expand/collapse toggle) — use a Cubit for anything shared
across widgets or that represents meaningful screen state.
Don't put business/UI logic directly in widgets — emit it from a Cubit and consume
it via BlocBuilder/BlocConsumer so widgets stay declarative and testable.
Don't hardcode colors, spacing, or font sizes inline — always reference
app_colors.dart / app_spacing.dart / app_typography.dart.
Don't create a vertical list for the Services section on Home — it must stay
horizontally scrollable per the approved design.
Don't introduce a dark navy (or any) solid-color card background on the Home hero
section — it must stay light/white, matching the rest of the app's cards.
Don't wire up the "Book Now" button to any action — it's UI-only per the task spec.
Don't add backend calls, HTTP clients, or persistence — dummy data only.
Don't use print() for debugging — use debugPrint() or remove before committing.
Don't leave any screen non-responsive — no fixed pixel widths that break on
smaller/larger devices.